WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.247
Neuroplasticity exists across the lifespan, but the conditions and speed of learning can vary.

2
00:00:06.247 --> 00:00:12.048
Childhood and adolescence include periods of rapid development and high responsiveness to experience.

3
00:00:12.048 --> 00:00:20.527
Some kinds of learning may have critical or sensitive periods, meaning developmental windows when certain adaptations are especially responsive.

4
00:00:20.527 --> 00:00:24.989
This does not mean learning ends when those windows close.

5
00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:28.113
Adults can continue learning and building skills.

6
00:00:28.113 --> 00:00:33.467
Prior knowledge, practice quality, motivation, feedback, health, environment, and recovery all matter.

7
00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:41.499
Adults may use different strategies than children because they bring more experience, stronger existing habits, and more responsibilities.

8
00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:44.623
That can create both advantages and barriers.

9
00:00:44.623 --> 00:00:51.316
Existing knowledge can help new learning attach, but old patterns may also need deliberate adjustment.

10
00:00:51.316 --> 00:00:55.779
Older learners can also continue adapting, though realistic expectations matter.

11
00:00:55.779 --> 00:01:02.026
Speed, energy, recovery needs, and prior experience may influence how practice should be designed.

12
00:01:02.026 --> 00:01:06.488
The useful message is neither extreme optimism nor deterministic pessimism.

13
00:01:06.488 --> 00:01:12.289
Age may shape the path, but it does not make meaningful learning impossible.

14
00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:16.752
Practice should be appropriate, sustainable, and connected to real goals.

15
00:01:16.752 --> 00:01:18.537
Avoid fixed-ability thinking.

16
00:01:18.537 --> 00:01:28.800
Saying, I am too old to learn, or I am just not that kind of person, can stop effort before evidence is gathered.

17
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:35.940
A better question is, what practice design, feedback, environment, and timeline would support this learner now?

18
00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:41.294
Lifespan plasticity is not a promise that every outcome is equally easy.

19
00:01:41.294 --> 00:01:46.649
It is a reminder that adaptation can continue when conditions support it.
